	(text "Power entry (top wall): one Amass XT per rail, board side male (PW-M).\nXT30 on +5V cannot mate with XT60. Pin 1 = GND, pin 2 = + per the KiCad\nfootprint. OPEN: the vendor STEP puts the angled end on pad 2; convention\nsays angled = minus. Check a real part before release."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 480.06 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e1a8e7f1-efbe-524e-8468-71a500e9c56d")
	)
	(text "Shack Relay Matrix, unit RF board, architecture rev C. One flat board in a milled 6082-T6 case.\nAll connectors are on this sheet: radio SO-239 J1 to J3 and EXP SMA J4 to J6 (left), antenna SO-239 J7 to J10\n(right), power J11 to J13. Unit 1: 3 radios x 4 antennas; A1 G5RV, A2 RX loop (RX only), A3 and A4 spare.\nCrossbar: the four vertical wires are the antenna columns ANT1 to ANT4 (L2). Each radio sheet holds\na TX row and an RX row (L1) with one relay per column. 37 x RT1: 3 K0, 15 TX, 15 RX, 4 K1; unit 1 fits 34 (no TX relay at A2, D-103).\nCoil drivers sit next to each relay; Rn_*_DRV and An_K1_DRV are 3.3 V gate inputs from the IO expanders sheet.\nJ14 goes to the controller board (unit 1) or takes the EXP ribbon from the unit 1 controller board (unit 2), D-51, D-53;\neach J14 signal passes the J14 filter sheet: series link, C footprint and test point (D-122, D-120).\nThe RF board is the same in both units. R1 K0 follows PTT in hardware (TX_ANY, R51, D-58); R2, R3 K0 from U903 (D-63).\nControl lines as buses (D-60): R1DRV to R3DRV (coil drives per radio), ANT (K1 drive, detector, bias feed per antenna port),\nCTRL (I2C, EXP_INT, RLY_EN). One bus segment at each block; the bus alias joins them, each entry wire carries its net name.\nTest: ERC; netlist check that each ANTk joins 6 row relays and one antenna port; logic verification (verify_logic.py, M-08).\nTarget: 50 ohm RF path, 100 W HF at SWR 3 (173 V peak, 2.45 A rms), PD3 outdoor box."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 243.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "45cd1b2d-a2ec-5cea-ba90-84e1dd5cf5db")
	)
